@subsection Remote mode (libreclaw 0.21.0+)

The remote-mode DEFUNs are available when both
@code{--with-cmacs-libreclaw} and @code{--with-cmacs-mcp} are
configured.  See @ref{LibreClaw Remote Mode} for the full narrative.

@table @code
@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote-connect URL &optional TOKEN
Elisp autoload, interactive.  Reads URL via @code{read-string} and
runs it through @code{cmacs-libreclaw-remote--normalize-url} so a
bare hostname like @code{libreclaw-00} expands to
@code{ws://libreclaw-00:7077/api/v1/bridge}.  @code{host:port},
@code{scheme://host}, and full URLs are also accepted.  If TOKEN
is nil it is fetched via @code{auth-source-search} keyed by the
normalised URL's host and port (offered for creation if absent).
Dispatches the underlying C bridge connect asynchronously.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote--normalize-url INPUT
Helper used by @code{cmacs-libreclaw-remote-connect}.  Expands
shorthand:
@itemize
@item INPUT with no scheme gets @code{ws://} prepended.
@item @code{ws://} URLs without an explicit port get @code{:7077}
appended.
@item @code{wss://} URLs without a port keep the scheme default
(443) --- typical for TLS-terminating reverse proxies.
@item URLs without a path or with only @code{/} get
@code{/api/v1/bridge} appended.
@end itemize

@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote--connect-internal URL TOKEN @
       &optional DISPLAY-NAME ENDPOINTS USER-ID
Internal C DEFUN.  Opens the bridge to URL with bearer TOKEN.
Optional DISPLAY-NAME identifies this client to the remote server.
Optional ENDPOINTS is a list of endpoint specs (only the symbol
@code{cmacs} is honoured in 0.21.0 --- wraps cmacs's own MCP tool
surface).  Default endpoint list is @code{(cmacs)}.  Optional
USER-ID is the @code{sender_id} stamped on every outbound
@code{chat.message_out} frame; match against the server's
@code{session.command_allowed_users} /
@code{messages.command_allowed_users} to enable session/message
bot commands.  When omitted the server falls back to the bridge id
(unstable across reconnects).

@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote-disconnect
Disconnect the remote bridge if any.  Safe to call twice.  Returns
@code{t} when something was disconnected, @code{nil} otherwise.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote-connected-p
Return non-nil if the remote bridge is connected.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote-send-message ROOM-ID BODY @
       &optional HTML-BODY
Send BODY to ROOM-ID over the remote bridge.  Returns @code{t} on
success, signals @code{cmacs-libreclaw-error} on failure.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote-status
Elisp interactive.  Prints a one-line status line to the
@code{*Messages*} buffer.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote-chat
Elisp autoload, interactive.  Opens (or pops to) the bridge's
local-style chat buffer @file{*libreclaw:bridge:local*}.
Equivalent to libreclaw's built-in local CLI channel, but flowing
over the bridge.  Idempotent --- multiple invocations reuse the
same buffer.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote-open-room ROOM-ID &optional ROOM-NAME
Elisp autoload, interactive.  Open or create a bridge room buffer
for ROOM-ID.  Useful for picking a specific room id on the remote
server.
@end table

@subsubsection Customisation

@table @code
@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote-mcp-servers
defcustom.  List of endpoint specs to expose to the remote libreclaw.
Default @code{(cmacs)}.  Future spec kinds (@code{:stdio CMD},
@code{:unix-socket PATH}, @code{:ws URL}) are reserved; unknown
entries are silently ignored.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote-display-name
defcustom.  Display name advertised to the remote server.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote-user-id
defcustom.  Default @code{nil}.  Stable @code{sender_id} stamped on
every outbound bridge chat frame; this is what the libreclaw
server's @code{session.command_allowed_users} and
@code{messages.command_allowed_users} lists match against.  When
@code{nil}, resolved at connect time to @code{$USER}, then
@code{(user-login-name)}, then to @code{nil} (server falls back to
the unstable bridge id).  Set explicitly for non-shell identities
(e.g. @code{"@@zach:matrix.example.com"}).  Reconnect for changes
to take effect.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote-local-room-id
defcustom.  Room id used by @code{cmacs-libreclaw-remote-chat}.
Default @code{"local"}.

@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote-local-room-name
defcustom.  Buffer display label for the local-style chat buffer.
Default @code{"Bridge"}.
@end table

@subsubsection Signal hooks

Called from C via the dispatch helper.  Override in user Elisp to
customise.

@table @code
@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote--on-chat-message CHANNEL ROOM SENDER BODY
@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote--on-room-added ROOM-ID
@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote--on-room-removed ROOM-ID
@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote--on-connected
@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote--on-disconnected
@item cmacs-libreclaw-remote--on-error MSG
@end table
